The gm-plugkit git_push verb (v0.1.553) hangs ~30s and returns ok:true with empty output WITHOUT actually pushing when the push needs interactive/SSH-agent credentials its subprocess cannot reach (github.com:AnEntrypoint/spoint.git over SSH). Symptom: git_push returns {ok:true,output:''} in exactly ~30115ms (a timeout, not a real push), but git rev-list --count origin/main..HEAD stays >0. WORKAROUND: after dispatching git_push, ALWAYS verify with git fetch origin <branch> + git rev-list --count origin/<branch>..HEAD == 0; if ahead>0, the verb silently failed — do a porcelain probe then raw git push origin <branch> (which reaches the credential cache) to actually land it. The verb's ok:true is not proof of remote landing on this repo.